"qa:bn:xorqa-bn-223,c6deb4b8714a7bda96c882c760202e1375cf30a5090c097a54263d016db693ee,qa,bn,Bengali,xorqa-bn-223,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Bengali. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""The Oxford Illustrated Companion to Medicine says that leprosy, as well as cures for it, were described in the Hindu religious book \\\""""Atharva-veda\\\"""". Writing in the \\\""""Encyclop¾dia Britannica 2008\\\"""", Kearns and Nash state that the first mention of leprosy is in the Indian medical treatise \\\""""Sushruta Samhita\\\"""" (6th century BC). \\\""""The Cambridge Encyclopedia of Human Paleopathology\\\"""" (1998) holds that: \\\""""The \\\""""Sushruta Samhita\\\"""" from India describes the condition quite well and even offers therapeutic suggestions as early as about 600 BC\\\"""" The surgeon Sushruta lived in the Indian city of Kashi by the 6th century BC, and the medical treatise \\\""""Sushruta Samhita\\\"""" attributed to him was documented during the 1st millennium BC. The earliest surviving excavated written material that contains the works of Sushruta is the \\\""""Bower Manuscript\\\""""Ñdated to the 4th century AD, almost a millennium after the original work. Despite these earlier works, Europeans believed that the first widely considered accurate description of the disease was that of Galen of Pergamum in 150 AD.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""________ ____ ____ _____ ____ ________ ___\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",_________,""*   Context: A paragraph discussing the history of leprosy mentions in various texts (Atharva-veda, Sushruta Samhita, Bower Manuscript, etc.)."
