"qa:kn:xorqa-kn-95,91fab552bdb5eea37102e6116c94fe2a43e2255e673cccb7864622b9fea94f1d,qa,kn,Kannada,xorqa-kn-95,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Kannada. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""The history of Buddism spans from the 5th century BCE to the present. Buddhism arose in the eastern part of Ancient India, in and around the ancient Kingdom of Magadha (now in Bihar, India), and is based on the teachings of Siddh_rtha Gautama. This makes it one of the oldest religions practiced today. The religion evolved as it spread from the northeastern region of the Indian subcontinent through Central, East, and Southeast Asia. At one time or another, it influenced most of the Asian continent. The history of Buddhism is also characterized by the development of numerous movements, schisms, and schools, among them the Therav_da, Mah_y_na and Vajray_na traditions, with contrasting periods of expansion and retreat.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""________ _____ ____ ___________ ?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",_________ ____.,""*   Context: A paragraph about the history and origins of Buddhism (5th century BCE, Magadha/Bihar, teachings of Siddh_rtha Gautama, spread through Asia, different schools like Therav_da, Mah_y_na, Vajray_na)."
"*   Question (in Kannada): """"________ _____ ____ ___________ ?"""" (Who founded Buddhism?)"
"*   Task: Answer the question using the context, in Kannada, concisely, and only explain if necessary."

"    *   Sentence 2: """"Buddhism arose in the eastern part of Ancient India... and is based on the teachings of Siddh_rtha Gautama."""""

