"qa:ml:xorqa-ml-110,2047c1902d2bb3d64bcb0a1bacd4a426ba764f886a0041a173ef7c95a0d98098,qa,ml,Malayalam,xorqa-ml-110,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Malayalam. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""The first documented account of the sliding rock phenomenon dates to 1915, when a prospector named Joseph Crook from Fallon, Nevada, visited the Racetrack Playa site. In the following years, the Racetrack sparked interest from geologists Jim McAllister and Allen Agnew, who mapped the bedrock of the area in 1948 and published the earliest report about the sliding rocks in a Geologic Society of America Bulletin. Their publication gave a brief description of the playa furrows and scrapers, stating that no exact measurements had been taken and suggesting that furrows were the remnants of scrapers propelled by strong gusts of wind Ð such as the variable winds that produce dust-devils Ð over a muddy playa floor. Controversy over the origin of the furrows prompted the search for the occurrence of similar phenomena at other locations. Such a location was found at Little Bonnie Claire Playa in Nye County, Nevada, and the phenomenon was studied there, as well.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""__________ _______ _____ ____________?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",1915-_ _____ ________ (Joseph Crook) ____ ______________ ___ _______ ________ ____________ ______ _______.,""*   Context: A text about the history of the sliding rock phenomenon at Racetrack Playa, mentioning Joseph Crook (prospector, 1915), Jim McAllister and Allen Agnew (geologists, 1948), and the phenomenon at Little Bonnie Claire Playa."
"*   Question: """"__________ _______ _____ ____________?"""" (Who discovered the sliding rocks?)"
"*   Task: Answer in Malayalam, concise, only include explanation if required."

"    *   """"The first documented account of the sliding rock phenomenon dates to 1915, when a prospector named Joseph Crook from Fallon, Nevada, visited the Racetrack Playa site."""" -> This implies Joseph Crook provided the first documented account."
"    *   """"In the following years, the Racetrack sparked interest from geologists Jim McAllister and Allen Agnew, who mapped... and published the earliest report..."""" -> They reported and studied it, but Crook provided the first account."

"    *   Question asks """"Who discovered the sliding rocks?"""""
"    *   The text says the """"first documented account... dates to 1915, when a prospector named Joseph Crook... visited the Racetrack Playa site."""""
"    *   So, Joseph Crook is the one associated with the first documented account."

    *   Answer: _____ ________ (Joseph Crook).
    *   Contextualizing: 1915-_ _____ ________ ____ ______________ ___ _______ ________ ____________ ______ _______. (A prospector named Joseph Crook gave the first documented account in 1915.)

    *   Concise answer: 1915-_ _____ ________ (Joseph Crook) ____ ______________ ___ _______ ________ ____________ ______ _______.

    *   Language: Malayalam.
    *   Concise: Yes.
    *   Use only supplied context: Yes.

"    *Draft:* 1915-_ _____ ________ (Joseph Crook) ____ ______________ ___ _______ ________ ____________ ______ _______."",025cf52ef1eacbfd39edf20970de6134d7c1c2b3f7745c7af380702620927de7,stop,""{""""completion_tokens"""":516,""""prompt_tokens"""":275,""""prompt_tokens_details"""":{""""cached_tokens"""":7},""""total_tokens"""":791}"",2026-10-19T12:00:38.030860+00:00"
"qa:ml:xorqa-ml-114,0e70c64d19eac2e1242dba9ad918083151e79bc38565d4e18b67522f14660072,qa,ml,Malayalam,xorqa-ml-114,gemma26b,494a4e4c54ae4f5b32ec6e0c7cc734f654652cba2d79b1246a5eb8f3f3508ec3,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Malayalam. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""Poultry is the second most widely eaten type of meat in the world, accounting for about 30% of total meat production worldwide compared to pork at 38%. Sixteen billion birds are raised annually for consumption, more than half of these in industrialised, factory-like production units. Global broiler meat production rose to 84.6 million tonnes in 2013. The largest producers were the United States (20%), China (16.6%), Brazil (15.1%) and the European Union (11.3%). There are two distinct models of production; the European Union supply chain model seeks to supply products which can be traced back to the farm of origin. This model faces the increasing costs of implementing additional food safety requirements, welfare issues and environmental regulations. In contrast, the United States model turns the product into a commodity.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""___ ___________ ______ _________ ______________?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",________ (20%) ___ _______ ____ ________ ______.,""*   Context: Information about poultry production (percentage of total meat, number of birds raised, top producers, production models)."
"*   Question: """"___ ___________ ______ _________ ______________?"""" (In which country are chickens most found/produced?)"
"*   Constraints: Use supplied context, respond in Malayalam, concise answer, include explanation only if required."

"    *   """"The largest producers were the United States (20%), China (16.6%), Brazil (15.1%) and the European Union (11.3%)."""""

