"qa:ml:xorqa-ml-79,38cba96a4cffcad33a385e18efe2c6330cfa6014d0e236536bfcf9ccca075a4a,qa,ml,Malayalam,xorqa-ml-79,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Malayalam. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""The Telugu year is the calendar year for the Telugu speaking people of . Each Yuga (Era) has a cycle of 60 years. Each year of Ugadi year has a specific name in Panchangam (Astrnomical calendar) based on astrological influences and the name of the year would represent the character of that year. The calendar includes 60 year names. Every 60 years one name cycle completes and the names repeat in the next cycle. For example, the Telugu name for 1954 is \\\""""jaya\\\"""", repeated in 2014. Ugadi is the Telugu new year festival that comes in the spring season (usually March or April). These years always change on Ugadi.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""________ ________ __________ ________ ______________ ___ ________ ___________?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",_______ __________ ______ _________.,""*   Context: Information about the Telugu year/calendar."
"    *   Question: """"________ ________ __________ ________ ______________ ___ ________ ___________?"""" (In which English month does the New Year start according to the Telugu Panchangam?)"
