"qa:pa:xorqa-pa-30,3f43c5f7279c9d702aab6820b8d0f88f51362faf2fb9fd7f2249232802c36be7,qa,pa,Punjabi,xorqa-pa-30,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Punjabi. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""Humans are generally diurnal. The average sleep requirement is between seven and nine hours per day for an adult and nine to ten hours per day for a child; elderly people usually sleep for six to seven hours. Having less sleep than this is common among humans, even though sleep deprivation can have negative health effects. A sustained restriction of adult sleep to four hours per day has been shown to correlate with changes in physiology and mental state, including reduced memory, fatigue, aggression, and bodily discomfort. During sleep humans dream. In dreaming humans experience sensory images and sounds, in a sequence which the dreamer usually perceives more as an apparent participant than as an observer. Dreaming is stimulated by the pons and mostly occurs during the REM phase of sleep.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""___ __ _____ ___ _____ ____ __ ____ __ ___ _____ __?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",""___ __ _____ __ ____ __ ___ ___ __ _____ ___ ___-___ _____ __: ______ __ 7 ___ 9 ____, ______ __ 9 ___ 10 ____, ___ ________ __ 6 ___ 7 _____"",""*   Context: Information about human sleep patterns (diurnal, adult sleep needs, child sleep needs, elderly sleep needs, effects of sleep deprivation, dreaming)."
