"*   Constraints: Concise answer, include explanation only if required, respond in Tamil."

"    *   """"In ancient Egypt, open (unframed) saws made of copper are documented as early as the Early Dynastic Period, circa 3,100Ð2,686 BC."""""
"    *   """"Many copper saws were found in tomb No. 3471 dating to the reign of Djer in the 31st century BC."""""

"    *   The context states that copper saws in ancient Egypt date back to the Early Dynastic Period, circa 3,100Ð2,686 BC."

"    *   Direct answer: ______ _________, ______ __.__. 3,100Ð2,686 ______________ ________ __ _________ _______. (In ancient Egypt, copper saws existed around 3,100-2,686 BC.)"
