"qa:te:xorqa-te-163,57500d2dbc7f2f04dcb759291833a5583d94430d8425ae7782d17b945c288686,qa,te,Telugu,xorqa-te-163,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Answer the question using the supplied context. Respond in Telugu. Give a concise answer; include an explanation only if the question requires one.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""context\"""": \""""According to Chaui, unlike the Western feminist movement, India's movement was initiated by men, and later joined by women. But feminism as an initiative by women started independently a little later in Maharashtra by pioneering advocates of women's rights and education: Savitribai Phule, who started the first school for girls in India (1848); Tarabai Shinde, who wrote India's first feminist text (1882); and Pandita Ramabai, who criticized patriarchy and caste-system in Hinduism, married outside her caste and converted to Christianity (1880s).  The efforts of Bengali reformers included abolishing sati, which was a widow's death by burning on her husband's funeral pyre, abolishing the custom of child marriage, abolishing the disfiguring of widows, introducing the marriage of upper caste Hindu widows, promoting women's education, obtaining legal rights for women to own property, and requiring the law to acknowledge women's status by granting them basic rights in matters such as adoption.\"""",\n  \""""question\"""": \""""__________ ______ ______ ____ _______ _____ ____ ____?\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",____________ ____.,""*   Context: A paragraph describing the history of feminism in India. It mentions Chaui's view (men started the movement, then women joined). It highlights women who started feminism independently in Maharashtra: Savitribai Phule (started the first school for girls in India in 1848), Tarabai Shinde (wrote India's first feminist text in 1882), and Pandita Ramabai (criticized patriarchy/caste in the 1880s). It also mentions Bengali reformers' efforts."
"    *   Question (in Telugu): """"__________ ______ ______ ____ _______ _____ ____ ____?"""" (Who was the first woman to fight for girls' rights in India?)"
