"    *   *Context:* Protests against the CAA in Uttar Pradesh, India."
    *   *Key Incident:* Mohammed Raees (a street hawker) was shot and died during a protest. His father feels targeted due to their religion.
    *   *Core Issue:* The CAA is seen by civil rights groups as discriminatory against Muslims (amnesty for non-Muslims from neighboring countries). The government denies this.
"    *   *Atmosphere in Muslim communities:* High fear of arrest, torture, and vandalism. Fear of NRC (National Register of Citizens) because of potential inability to prove citizenship."
    *   *Allegations against Police/State:* Disproportionate force used; night-time raids; vandalism of Muslim homes/property; extrajudicial killings/shootings; intimidation.
