"*   Input Document: An article about the Indian government's demonetization move (scrapping 500 and 1,000 rupee notes to fight black money)."

"    *   *Event:* The Indian government announced the removal of 500 and 1,000 rupee notes from circulation (demonetization)."
    *   *Reason:* To combat corruption and illegal cash holdings (black money).
"    *   *Immediate Impact:* Banks closed on Wednesday, ATMs non-functional, limits on cash withdrawals."
"    *   *Process:* New 500 and 2,000 rupee notes will be issued. Old notes can be exchanged at banks (dates: 10 Nov - 30 Dec), but they are no longer legal tender."
    *   *Implications/Analysis:*
"        *   Aims to make """"black money"""" visible for tax purposes."
        *   Banks will monitor large exchanges.
"        *   Potential deflationary impact (e.g., real estate)."
        *   Risk: Impact on small traders/cash-heavy economy and short-term economic uncertainty.
"    *   *Key Figures:* PM Modi, Finance Secretary Shaktikant Das, Simon Jack (BBC)."

"    *   *Central Message:* The Indian government has taken a major step to fight corruption and black money by scrapping high-denomination notes (500 and 1,000 rupees)."
    *   *Supporting Details:*
"        *   New notes (500 and 2,000) will be introduced."
        *   Old notes must be exchanged at banks within a specific timeframe (until Dec 30).
        *   Banks will closely monitor large transactions.
"        *   The move has caused immediate chaos (ATM/Bank closures) and economic uncertainty, especially for those relying on cash."

