    *   *Topic:* Diabetes classification (beyond Type 1 and Type 2).
"    *   *Key Research:* Study by Lund University (Sweden) and Institute for Molecular Medicine (Finland) on 14,775 patients."
    *   *Findings:* Patients can be divided into five distinct clusters instead of just two types.
"    *   *Implication:* This enables """"precision medicine"""" or """"personalized medicine."""""
    *   *Details of Clusters:*
        *   Some clusters need more aggressive treatment.
"        *   Cluster 2 might be caused by beta-cell defects rather than lifestyle/fat, needing treatment more like Type 1."
        *   Cluster 2 has a higher blindness risk; Cluster 3 has a higher kidney disease risk (need for enhanced screening).
    *   *Expert Opinions:*
        *   Prof Leif Groop: Big step toward precision medicine.
"        *   Dr. Victoria Salem: Reflects future of diabetes care, but current practice won't change immediately (study was on Scandinavians, risks vary globally)."
