"    *   *Main Subject:* Dennis Aabo, a Danish man who lost his hand in a firework accident."
    *   *The Innovation:* A bionic hand that provides real-time touch sensation (sensory feedback) to the brain.
    *   *The Method:* Sensors in the prosthetic hand detect touch/pressure $\rightarrow$ electrical signals $\rightarrow$ computer algorithms $\rightarrow$ impulses sent to nerves in the upper arm via implanted electrodes $\rightarrow$ brain interprets touch.
"    *   *The Team:* International group (Italy, Switzerland, Germany) including neuroscientists, engineers, surgeons."
"    *   *Results:* Aabo could feel shapes and textures (hard/soft, round/square) even while blindfolded."
    *   *Current Status:* It's a prototype. Aabo underwent two surgeries. Sensors were removed due to clinical trial safety rules.
"    *   *Future Outlook:* Goal is to miniaturize the tech (no external cables), make it fully implantable, and eventually include texture/temperature. It's likely a decade away from commercial availability and will be expensive."

