"    *   Input Data (JSON): A text about legal proceedings in Egypt involving supporters of ousted President Mohammed Morsi, specifically regarding the Kerdasa deaths and ongoing espionage trials."

    *   *Key Fact 1:* Men were convicted for the deaths of at least 11 officers in Kerdasa (after military crackdown on Morsi supporters).
"    *   *Key Fact 2:* Hundreds of death sentences were passed on Morsi's supporters, but none carried out yet."
    *   *Key Fact 3:* Amnesty International claims trials were unfair and violate international law.
    *   *Key Fact 4:* Mohammed Morsi faces a new espionage trial (Feb 15) regarding leaking documents to Qatar/Al-Jazeera. He already has three other trials.
"    *   *Key Fact 5:* In the Kerdasa case, over 140 are in custody, some sentenced in absentia. A minor got 10 years; two acquitted. Verdict follows Grand Mufti's recommendation but can be appealed."
"    *   *Key Fact 6:* UN calls mass trials """"unprecedented."""""
