    *   *Winners:*
"        *   Olga Tokarczuk (awarded the 2018 prize): Polish novelist, known for blending real and mystical, works like *Primeval and Other Times*, *The Books of Jacob*. 15th female winner."
        *   Peter Handke (awarded the 2019 prize): Austrian playwright/novelist/poet. Recognized for influential work exploring human experience. Highly controversial due to support for Serbs/Milosevic during the Yugoslav war.
    *   *Controversies:* Handke has faced criticism for denying the Srebrenica massacre and comparing Serbia's fate to the Holocaust. PEN America criticized his selection.
