"    *   *Core Message:* A report (by Institute on Medicine as a Profession and Open Society Foundations) alleges that US medical professionals helped design and participate in the torture and inhumane treatment of detainees (Guantanamo, Afghanistan, CIA sites)."
    *   *Key Findings of the report:*
        *   Medical professionals helped facilitate abuse.
        *   Ethical standards were changed to allow this.
"        *   Specific practices mentioned: Force-feeding, using coercive restraint chairs, and searching for vulnerabilities in interrogations."
    *   *Reactions:*
        *   CIA and Pentagon reject the report.
        *   CIA claims inaccuracies and notes they no longer hold detainees and the program was ended in 2009.
"        *   Pentagon defends the medical professionals, calling them """"consummate professionals"""" and saying they provide excellent care."
    *   *Recommendation of the report:* US Senate Intelligence Committee should investigate medical practices at detention sites.

    *   *Central Message:* __ _______ ___ ____ _____ ___ __ __ _______ ________ ________ __ _______ __ ___ ____ ____ __________ __ _______ _________ ___ ___ __ ___ (A report alleges that US medical professionals helped in torture and inhumane treatment of detainees.)
"    *   *Supporting Info (Report details):* __ _______ _____ __ __ _________ ________ __ ______ __ ___ _________ __ _____ ____ __ ____ ____ _____ (force-feeding) ____ _______ ___ ___ ____, __ _____ ______ __ _____ ____ (The report states that health professionals participated in practices like identifying vulnerabilities for interrogation and force-feeding, which violate ethical standards.)"
"    *   *Reactions:* _______, _____ (CIA) __ _______ __ __ __________ __ _____ __ ____ ___ _____ __ ___ ___ _____ __, ____ _______ __ ________ ________ __ ______ _______ __ ____ ____ ___ (However, CIA and Pentagon have rejected these findings. CIA called it incorrect, while Pentagon defended the professional conduct of medical personnel.)"

