"    *   *Central Message:* US researchers found that dolphins can remember the """"signature whistles"""" of former companions even after 20 years of separation."
    *   *Study Details:*
        *   Researchers: Dr. Jason Bruck (University of Chicago) and others.
        *   Published in: *Proceedings of the Royal Society B*.
        *   Subjects: 56 captive bottlenose dolphins from US and Bermuda zoos/aquariums.
        *   Method: Played recordings of former companions' whistles; dolphins responded by approaching speakers more often/longer.
        *   Key finding: Unprecedented long-term memory in animal behavior. Example: Bailey responded to Allie after 20+ years.
    *   *Reasoning/Mechanism:*
"        *   Driven by complex """"fission-fusion"""" social structures (moving between groups)."
        *   Helps them decide whether to approach or avoid individuals in the wild.
"    *   *Cognitive Level:* Comparable to humans, chimpanzees, and elephants."
"    *   *Distinction:* Unlike elephants (who mostly remember family), dolphins remember both family and former acquaintances."
"    *   *Additional Note:* Dolphins have """"signature whistles"""" similar to human names."

"    *   *Draft 1 (Mental):* US ke researchers ne bataya ki dolphins apne purane doston ki whistles 20 saal baad bhi yaad rakh sakte hain. Ye study Proceedings of the Royal Society B mein chhapi. 56 dolphins par research hui. Dolphins ne unki awaaz par zyada response diya jinhe wo pehle jante the. Iska karan unka """"fission-fusion"""" social structure hai. Inki yaadshakti insaano, chimpanzees aur elephants jaisi hai."

