"    *   *The Surprise:* Scientists thought solar winds (which bring magnetic shielding) would *decrease* lightning by blocking cosmic rays. Instead, they *increase* lightning."
"    *   *Data/Evidence:* In Northern Europe, strikes increased from 321 (40 days prior) to 422 (40 days after) high-speed wind arrival."
"    *   *Predictability:* Solar wind streams are predictable (Sun rotates every 27 days), which could help in forecasting lightning storms."
"    *   *Scope:* Data was from Europe, but the effect is likely global."

