"summarization:hi:crosssum-hi-81,2081bd6cb928b1447ff40b8890d15c9c573511f703f08cddc123fece52013c6b,summarization,hi,Hindi,crosssum-hi-81,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Summarize the supplied document in Hindi. Give a concise summary of the central message and essential supporting information. Do not add unsupported facts. Return only the summary.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""document\"""": \""""The flaw affects Internet Explorer (IE) versions 6 to 11 and Microsoft said it was aware of \\\""""limited, targeted attacks\\\"""" to exploit it. According to NetMarket Share, the IE versions account for more than 50% of global browser market. Microsoft says it is investigating the flaw and will take \\\""""appropriate\\\"""" steps. The firm, which issued a security advisory over the weekend, said the steps \\\""""may include providing a solution through our monthly security update release process, or an out-of-cycle security update, depending on customer needs\\\"""". The US government advised computer users to consider using alternative web browsers until a security fix is released. XP impact However, the issue may be of special concern to people still using the Windows XP operating system. That is because Microsoft ended official support for that system earlier this month. It means there will be no more official security updates and bug fixes for XP from the firm. Cyber security firm Symantec said it had carried out tests which confirmed that \\\""""the vulnerability crashes Internet Explorer on Windows XP\\\"""". \\\""""This will be the first zero day vulnerability that will not be patched for Windows XP users,\\\"""" it added. About 30% of all desktops are thought to be still running Windows XP and analysts have previously warned that those users would be vulnerable to attacks from cyber-thieves. Microsoft has suggested businesses and consumers still using the system should upgrade to a newer alternative. 'Complete control' Microsoft said that hackers looking to exploit the flaw could host a \\\""""specially crafted website\\\"""" containing content that can help them do so. However, they would still need to convince users to view the website for them to be able to gain access to their computer. They could do this by getting them to click on a link sent via an email or instant messenger, or by opening an attachment sent through an email. However, a hacker would have \\\""""no way to force users\\\"""" to view the content. If successful, a hacker could gain the same rights as the computer's current user. \\\""""If the current user is logged on with administrative user rights, an attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could take complete control of an affected system,\\\"""" the firm warned. \\\""""An attacker could then install programs; view, change, or delete data; or create new accounts with full user rights.\\\"""" But the firm added that Internet Explorer on Windows Server 2003, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2008 R2, Windows Server 2012, and Windows Server 2012 R2 runs in a restricted mode, which \\\""""mitigates this vulnerability\\\"""".\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",""_______ __________ (IE) __ _______ 6 __ 11 ___ __ _______ ____ ___ __ __, _____ _____ ____ ______ ____________ __ ________ __ _____ ________ _______ __ ____ ____ ____________ __ ______ __ ____ __ ___ __ __ ____ __ _______ _____ ____ ____ __ _______ ___ _______ _____ __ _______ _____ ___ __ ________ ________ _____ ____ __ ____ __ ___ ____ ____ _____ __ ____________ __ ___ __ __ Windows XP __ _____ __ ___ ___, _______ ____________ __ __ ______ __ ___ ___ _______ _____ ____ ____ ______ ______ __ ____ __ ___ _____ __ ___ ______ ____ __ ____ __ ______ __ ____________ __ _____ ___ __ ____ __ ______________ _________ __ __ ____ __ ______ __ ____ ____ _______, ______ _____ __ _______ _______ '_____________ ___' __ ____ __ ____ __ ____ __ __ ________ ____"",""*   Task: Summarize the provided document."
    *   Language: Hindi.
    *   Content requirements: Concise summary of the central message and essential supporting information. No unsupported facts.
    *   Output format: Return *only* the summary.
    *   Input data (JSON): A text about a security flaw in Internet Explorer (IE) versions 6-11.

    *   *Topic:* Security flaw in Internet Explorer (IE) versions 6-11.
"    *   *Impact:* Affects >50% of global browser market. Microsoft is aware of """"limited, targeted attacks."""""
    *   *Microsoft's Response:* Investigating; may provide a solution via monthly updates or an out-of-cycle update.
    *   *US Government Advice:* Use alternative browsers until a fix is released.
"    *   *Windows XP specific risk:* Major concern for XP users because Microsoft ended support earlier this month (no more official security updates/patches). Symantec confirmed it crashes IE on XP. This is the first """"zero-day"""" vulnerability that won't be patched for XP. ~30% of desktops use XP. Microsoft suggests upgrading."
"    *   *How it works:* Hackers use """"specially crafted websites."""" Users must be tricked into visiting (via email/IM links/attachments)."
"    *   *Consequences:* If successful, hacker gets user's rights. If admin, they get """"complete control"""" (install programs, delete data, create accounts)."
"    *   *Mitigation:* Windows Server versions (2003-2012 R2) run in """"restricted mode,"""" which mitigates the vulnerability."

    *   *Central Message:* Internet Explorer (IE) versions 6-11 have a security flaw that allows hackers to take control of systems if users visit malicious websites.
    *   *Key Points:*
        1.  Microsoft is investigating and will release updates.
        2.  US government advises using other browsers.
        3.  Windows XP users are at high risk because XP no longer gets security updates.
        4.  Hackers need users to click links/attachments to exploit it.
        5.  Successful exploitation gives attackers user/admin rights (full control).
"        6.  Windows Server versions are largely protected by """"restricted mode."""""

"    *   *Draft 1 (Mental):* Internet Explorer (IE) ke version 6 se 11 tak mein ek security flaw mila hai. Microsoft ise theek karne ke liye kaam kar raha hai. US sarkar ne dusre browsers use karne ki salah di hai. Sabse bada khatra Windows XP users ke liye hai kyunki uske liye koi update nahi aayega. Hackers malicious links ke zariye users ko fasakar unke computer ka pura control le sakte hain. Halanki, Windows Server versions isse surakshit hain."

    *   *Draft 2 (More formal and concise):*
"        _______ __________ (IE) __ _______ 6 __ 11 ___ __ _______ ____ ___ __ __, _____ _____ _____ ______ ____________ __ ________ __ _____ ________ _______ __ ____ ____ ____________ __ ______ __ ____ __ ___ __ __ _____ ____ ______ _______ _____ __ _______ _____ ___ __ ________ ________ _____ ____ __ ____ __ ___ ____ ____ _____ Windows XP ____________ __ ___ __, _______ ____________ __ __ ______ __ ___ _______ _____ ____ ____ ______ ______ __ ____ __ ___ _____ __ ___ _____ ___ __ ____ __ _________ __ ______ ____ __ _____ __ ____ ____ _______, ______ _____ __ _______ _______ '_____________ ___' __ ____ __ ____ __ ____ __ __ ________ ____"

    *   Does it summarize the central message? Yes.
