"    *   Input: A text about a record-breaking heatwave in the US (specifically Death Valley), its causes/context, current effects (blackouts, firenado), and general health/infrastructure impacts."

    *   *Main Event:* US National Weather Service is verifying a record-breaking temperature reading in Death Valley.
    *   *Context:* Heatwave on the US west coast (AZ to WA).
    *   *Record Details:* Previous reliable record: 129.2¡F (54¡C) in Death Valley (2013). A higher reading (134¡F) in 1913 is disputed.
"    *   *Current Situation:* Severe heat in California, power plant malfunction, Stage 3 Emergency declared, rolling blackouts to manage demand/supply (especially with high AC use and solar/wind reliance)."
"    *   *Other Phenomena:* """"Firenado"""" in Lassen County."
"    *   *Health Impacts:* Heat cramps, dehydration, heat stroke, worsening of pre-existing conditions (heart, respiratory, kidney)."
"    *   *Infrastructure/Other Impacts:* Power grid strain, plane grounding, melting roads, car overheating, agricultural damage (wilting, plant diseases)."

"    *   *Central Message:* The US West Coast is experiencing an extreme heatwave, with record-breaking temperatures being verified in Death Valley, causing significant power grid issues and health/infrastructure risks."

    *   *Supporting Info:*
        *   Death Valley temperature record under verification (previously 54¡C in 2013).
        *   California facing Stage 3 energy emergency and blackouts due to high demand for AC.
"        *   Heatwaves cause health problems (dehydration, heatstroke) and damage infrastructure (roads, power grids, agriculture)."

