"    *   *Location:* Jenggot, south of Pekalongan, Central Java."
    *   *Cause:* Flooding hit the local batik dye production area.
    *   *Visuals:* Social media showed colored water; confirmed by local official (Dimas Arga Yudha).
"    *   *Context:* Pekalongan's rivers have turned different colors (e.g., green) before due to batik dyes."
"    *   *Broader Context:* Indonesia faces frequent flooding (e.g., Jakarta storm caused 43 deaths). Authorities used cloud seeding to prevent rain in recent worst floods since 2013."

"    *   *Central Message:* Flooding in Jenggot, Central Java, caused crimson batik dye to spill into the streets and rivers."
