"    *   *Section 1 (Main News):* Heatwave affecting ~200 million people in the US East Coast (NY, DC, Boston) and Midwest, plus parts of Canada. Temperatures near/exceeding 100F (38C). Experts link this to climate change. The world had its hottest June on record. Alaska also saw record highs."
"    *   *Section 2 (Specific Heatwave Info):* Areas affected: Central Plains (CO, KS) to Great Lakes. NY Mayor declared a local emergency, opened cooling centers, urged people to stay hydrated/stay indoors. Canada (Quebec, Ontario, Nova Scotia) issued heat warnings."
    *   *Section 3 (Forecast):* Heatwave expected to continue through the weekend. Temperatures might feel like Death Valley. A dramatic cool-down is expected early next week.
"    *   *Section 4 (Glossary/Background):* Extensive list of climate change terms (1.5 degrees, 2 degrees, 3 degrees, 4 degrees, Adaptation, AGW, Arctic ice, Attribution, Average temperature, BECCS, Biofuel, Biomass, Carbon, Carbon capture, Carbon dioxide, Carbon footprint, Carbon neutral, Carbon offsetting, Carbon sink, CCU, Climate change, Climate model, Climate negotiations, CO2, COP, Copenhagen, Coral bleaching, Deforestation, Deniers, Emissions, Extreme weather, Feedback loop, Fossil fuels, Geo-engineering, Global temperature, Global warming, Green energy, Greenhouse gases, Gulf Stream, Hydrocarbon, IPCC, Jetstream, Kyoto Protocol, Lukewarmers, Methane, Mitigation, Net zero, Ocean acidification, Ozone layer, PPM, Pre-industrial, Renewable energy, Runaway climate change, Sea ice, Sea level rises, Sustainability, Tipping point, UNFCCC)."

