    *   *Main Topic:* Formation of the International Alliance for Cancer Early Detection.
"    *   *Participants:* Cancer Research UK, Universities (Cambridge, Manchester, UCL), US institutions (Stanford, Oregon)."
"    *   *Goal:* Early detection of cancer to improve patient outcomes and reduce costs (from """"firefighting"""" late-stage disease to early intervention)."
    *   *Methods/Research Areas:*
"        *   Growing cancer in labs (using human tissue/synthetic immune cells) to see its """"birth."""""
"        *   Developing less invasive tests (blood, breath, urine)."
"        *   Improving imaging techniques (MRI, photoacoustics) to avoid biopsies."
        *   Developing advanced endoscopes.
        *   Considering genetics and environment for personal risk assessment.
