"    *   *Event:* Alan Henning, a 47-year-old British taxi driver/aid worker, was kidnapped by IS in Syria while delivering aid in December."
    *   *The Incident:* A video surfaced (though unverified at the time of report) appearing to show his execution. The video also threatened US aid worker Peter Kassig.
"    *   *Political Reaction:* UK PM David Cameron condemned the """"barbaric"""" act, vowed to bring killers to justice, and noted it reinforces the need for UK intervention against IS. US President Obama also condemned it."
"    *   *Family/Friends:* Mrs. Barbara Henning appealed for his release, stating he was innocent and doing good work. Friends described him as selfless and courageous."
"    *   *Broader Context:* IS has a history of killing hostages (James Foley, Steven Sotloff, David Haines). The UK is involved in military strikes against IS in Iraq."
"    *   *Analysis Note:* While leaders promise justice, historical precedent shows it's rare to catch/prosecute such killers in the UK."

    *   *Central Message:* The brutal killing of British aid worker Alan Henning by IS in Syria has sparked widespread condemnation from international leaders and highlights the brutality of the terrorist group.

