"    *   *Subject:* S.P. Balasubrahmanyam (SPB), a legendary playback singer."
    *   *Death:* Died on Friday due to cardio-respiratory arrest after battling Covid-19.
    *   *Career Highlights:*
        *   Sang in 16 languages.
        *   Known for hits in South Indian and Bollywood films.
        *   First crossover singer (South to Bollywood).
        *   Breakthrough Bollywood film: *Ek Duuje Ke Liye* (1981).
        *   Worked with top composers like AR Rahman and Ilaiyaraaja.
"        *   Singing style: Versatile (romantic, classical, yodelling, dance tracks)."
"        *   Prolific: Recorded many songs a day (sometimes 21 in Kannada, sometimes 17 in a day)."
"        *   Background: Born in 1946, Nellore; dropped out of engineering to pursue music."
"        *   Awards: Padma Shri (2001), Padma Bhushan (2011)."
"        *   Personal: High popularity (fans wrote letters in blood), had unique habits (smoking/cold drinks)."

"    *   *Central Message:* S.P. Balasubrahmanyam, a legendary playback singer who sang in 16 languages and bridged the gap between South Indian and Bollywood cinema, has passed away due to cardio-respiratory arrest following Covid-19."
