"*   Input Format: JSON containing the """"document""""."

"    *   *Main Topic:* Rapid decline of insects (bees, ants, beetles) compared to other animals."
    *   *Key Findings:* Insects are disappearing 8x faster than mammals/birds/reptiles. 40% of insect species might go extinct in the next few decades. 1/3 are already endangered.
"    *   *Causes:* Intensive agriculture (habitat loss, deforestation, urbanization), pesticides/fertilizers, chemical pollution, invasive species/pathogens, and climate change (especially in tropics)."
"    *   *Impacts:* Disruption of food chains (affects birds, reptiles, fish), loss of pollination (75% of crops rely on it), loss of soil replenishment (dung beetles), and loss of pest control."
"    *   *The """"Winners"""":* Pests like houseflies and cockroaches (fast breeders, adaptable to humans, pesticide-resistant) might thrive."
"    *   *Solutions/Needs:* More research (especially in Africa/South America), making gardens insect-friendly, avoiding pesticides, buying organic."
"    *   *Long-term view:* New species might evolve eventually, but it takes millions of years."

