    *   *Diplomacy:* Both sides accusing each other of violating agreements. High-level meetings held; attempts at de-escalation.
"    *   *Long-term impact:* Shift from relatively stable rivalry to heightened mistrust and antagonism; end of """"bonhomie"""" (friendship/goodwill) seen in previous summits."
"    *   *Key figures/experts mentioned:* Dr. Narang (MIT), Shashank Joshi (The Economist), Ajai Shukla (Defence Analyst), Ankit Panda (The Diplomat), Shivshankar Menon (former NSA), Karan Thapar."

"    *   *Central Message:* The recent violent clash in the Galwan Valley between India and China is a significant escalation in their long-standing border dispute, leading to casualties and a shift towards deeper mistrust between the two nations."

    *   *Supporting Details:*
