"    *   *Subject:* Takahiro Shiraishi (""""Twitter killer"""")."
"    *   *Crime:* Murdered and dismembered 8 women and 1 man (aged 15-26) between Aug-Oct 2017. He used Twitter to lure suicidal women to his flat in Zama, Japan."
    *   *Arrest:* Arrested in 2017 after body parts were found in his flat (following a missing person report).
"    *   *Trial:* Prosecutors sought the death penalty. Defense argued """"murder with consent,"""" but Shiraishi later denied this, and the judge ruled no consent was given."
"    *   *Verdict:* Judge Naokuni Yano called the crimes """"cunning and cruel"""" and found him fully responsible."
    *   *Sentence:* Death penalty (hanging).
    *   *Societal Impact:* Triggered debate on online discussions about suicide; Twitter updated rules to forbid promoting suicide/self-harm; Japan's suicide rates and online regulation are concerns.
    *   *Victims' Families:* Expressed profound grief and called the sentence appropriate.

