"*   Requirements: Concise summary, central message, essential supporting information, no unsupported facts, return *only* the summary."

"    *   *Core Subject:* A global study (Wellcome Trust) of 140,000+ people in 140+ countries regarding vaccine confidence."
"    *   *Main Finding:* Confidence in vaccines is low in some regions, posing a threat to global health."
    *   *Key Issue:* Vaccine hesitancy (fear/misinformation) is causing resurgences of diseases like measles.
    *   *Scientific Context:* Vaccines are the best defense; they've eradicated smallpox and are close to eliminating polio.
    *   *Specific Data points:*
"        *   High-income regions (e.g., France, parts of Europe, North America) show lower confidence in vaccine safety/effectiveness."
