"        In India, the growth of digital streaming (OTT) is revolutionizing the entertainment industry. It offers creative freedom to directors to tell stories (like LGBTQ+ themes) that are often censored on TV or in movies. It also provides new opportunities for actors and writers who were previously limited by the mainstream system. Global players like Netflix and Amazon are investing in India. The business model relies on direct subscriptions and affordable mobile data. While challenges like pricing and content targeting exist, the boom offers hope to many professionals in Mumbai."

