"*   Input: A text about the naval incident in the Kerch Strait involving Russia and Ukraine, Poroshenko's response, and NATO/international reactions."

    *   *Central Incident:* Russia seized three Ukrainian ships and their crews in the Kerch Strait (between the Black Sea and Sea of Azov).
    *   *Ukraine's Stance (Poroshenko):* Accuses Putin of wanting to occupy the Sea of Azov; requests NATO/Germany to relocate naval ships to the Sea of Azov for security. Implemented martial law in border regions.
"    *   *Russia's Stance (Putin):* Calls it a """"provocation"""" by Poroshenko to boost election ratings; claims Ukraine """"trespassed"""" into Russian waters; calls martial law extreme."
"    *   *NATO's Stance:* Expresses """"full support"""" for Ukraine; increased presence in the Black Sea; unlikely to deploy ships to the Sea of Azov due to legal/practical reasons and fear of escalating tensions."
    *   *International Reaction:* EU condemned Russia but failed to agree on new sanctions; US (Trump) might cancel a meeting with Putin; Western governments back Ukraine's sovereignty.
    *   *Context:* Kerch Strait/Crimea annexation history; tension over maritime access.

"    *   *Central Message:* _____ _______ ________ ______ _______ ___________ ______ ____________ _____________ _______, _______ ______ __________, __________ _____ ______ (NATO) _______ _________ ______ ________ _____ ________ ______________. (Russia seized Ukrainian ships/crew; Poroshenko asks NATO for naval protection)."

    *   *Supporting Info 1 (Poroshenko's View):* ______ _____ ____ ___________ ___________ _____ __________ _______ __________. (Putin wants to occupy Azov Sea).
