    *   Input Data: A text about Bongekile Msibi and 47 other women in South Africa who were sterilized without consent at state hospitals.

    *   *Core Event:* The Commission for Gender Equality found that 48 women (including Bongekile Msibi) were sterilized without consent in South African state hospitals.
"    *   *The Victim's Story:* Msibi discovered 11 years later she had no uterus. A doctor claimed it was to save her life and that her mother signed consent, but both claims are disputed. She lost her ability to have children and faced personal life consequences (breakup, emotional pain)."
"    *   *Commission Findings:* Inquiry was difficult because files """"disappeared"""" and hospital staff were """"hostile."""" The investigation spanned 15 hospitals and cases dating back to 2001."
    *   *Health Department Response:* No detailed response yet; the minister requested a meeting.
"    *   *Victim's Demands:* Accountability, an apology, and financial support for surrogacy."

    *   *Central Message:* ____________________ 48 _______ ___________ _______ _______ ______ ______________ _______ _____ ________ (sterilization) __________________ _____ _______ ______ __________________. (The Commission for Gender Equality has found that 48 women in South Africa underwent sterilization/hysterectomy without consent.)

    *   *Supporting Details:*
"        *   Bongekile Msibi's case: She found out 11 years later she had no uterus. The doctor claimed it was to save her life and her mother signed, but she denies this."
