    *   *Core Event:* Allegations that Jeff Bezos' phone was hacked via a WhatsApp message from Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman's personal account in May 2018.
"    *   *Method:* An infected video file sent via WhatsApp contained malware, allowing access to GPS, camera, banking, and messages."
    *   *Context/Motive:* Relations between Saudi Arabia and Bezos (owner of Washington Post) soured after the murder of Jamal Khashoggi (a critic) in a Saudi consulate. Bezos suggested Saudi Arabia was unhappy with the Post's coverage.
"    *   *Denials:* Saudi US embassy called the reports """"absurd"""" and denied claims via Twitter. Amazon did not respond."
    *   *Investigation:* The allegations stem from an investigation commissioned by Bezos (FTI Consulting). UN officials were expected to comment.
"    *   *Historical Context:* Bezos previously accused the National Enquirer of blackmail regarding leaked private texts, which his investigator linked to Saudi involvement."

"    *   *Central Message:* Jeff Bezos' phone was allegedly hacked via a WhatsApp message from Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman's account, potentially linked to the Washington Post's coverage of Jamal Khashoggi's murder."
    *   *Supporting Info:*
        *   The hack involved an infected video file that allowed access to sensitive phone data.
"        *   Saudi Arabia's US embassy has denied these claims, calling them """"absurd."""""
        *   The investigation was commissioned by Bezos through FTI Consulting.
        *   The incident follows tensions regarding the death of Jamal Khashoggi and previous leaks involving the National Enquirer.

"    *   *Central Message:* _____ ________ (Jeff Bezos) ____, _____ _______ ______ ____ _________ _______ (WhatsApp) ______________ ____ ___ ______ ______ _____ ____ ________________ _____________. ___ _________ ______ _______ _____ _______ __________ _________ _______________ _______ __________ _____ ____________________. (Jeff Bezos's phone was allegedly hacked through a video file from Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman's WhatsApp account. It is suspected this could be due to Washington Post's coverage of Jamal Khashoggi's murder.)"

