"*   Input: A text describing the launch of the iPhone X, iPhone 8, iPhone 8 Plus, Apple Watch Series 3 (with 4G), and updates to Apple TV (4K/HDR)."

"    *   *iPhone X:* Uses FaceID (facial recognition) instead of TouchID. Features OLED display, wireless charging, no home button. Prices: $999 (64GB), $1149 (256GB). It's a template for future hardware."
    *   *iPhone 8 / 8 Plus:* Prices $699-$849 (8) and $799-$949 (8 Plus). Support for wireless charging.
"    *   *FaceID vs. TouchID:* FaceID is more secure (1 in 1 million chance of being fooled vs. 1 in 50,000 for TouchID). Some users might miss the fingerprint sensor."
    *   *iOS 11 & AR:* Introduces ARKit for augmented reality.
    *   *Apple Watch Series 3:* New version with 4G/LTE (can work without an iPhone). Includes heart rate monitoring features (detecting irregular rhythms). Price: $399.
    *   *Apple TV:* Now supports 4K and HDR. Movies in HDR won't cost more than HD.
    *   *Market Context:* Apple is increasing prices (iPhone X is the most expensive yet) to meet shareholder expectations and manage demand.

"    *   *Central Message:* Apple has unveiled the iPhone X, featuring FaceID and an OLED display, alongside the iPhone 8 series, a new 4G-capable Apple Watch, and 4K-enabled Apple TV."
    *   *Key Supporting Details:*
