"    *   *Human Rights Perspective:* Amnesty International calls it a """"travesty of justice"""" and an attempt to silence dissent. They view him as a """"prisoner of conscience."""""
    *   *Historical Context:* 2011 pro-democracy protests (Shia-led) were suppressed by the Sunni-led Al Khalifa monarchy with help from Saudi Arabia.
    *   *Political Landscape:* Bahrain is a key US/UK ally. The country has seen crackdowns on opposition groups (Al-Wefaq banned) and imprisonment of critics.
"    *   *Key Players:* Sheikh Ali Salman, Hassan Sultan, Ali al-Aswad, Amnesty International, Qatar, Bahraini government."

"    *   *Central Message:* Sheikh Ali Salman, leader of the banned Al-Wefaq party, has been sentenced to life imprisonment by Bahraini authorities for allegedly conspiring with Qatar to overthrow the government, a move criticized by human rights groups as an attempt to suppress dissent."

