"    *   Input: A text about Prof. Richard Thaler winning the Nobel Prize in Economics for his work on """"nudge theory"""" and behavioral economics."

    *   *Subject:* Prof. Richard Thaler (Chicago Booth business school).
    *   *Achievement:* Won the Nobel Prize in Economics (Sveriges Riksbank Prize).
"    *   *Core Concept:* """"Nudge theory"""" and """"Behavioral Economics."""""
"    *   *Key Findings:* People are often irrational in decision-making (choosing what's easy over what's wise, even if it's bad for them)."
"    *   *Practical Application:* """"Nudging"""" helps people make better choices (e.g., saving for pensions, healthy eating) by subtly influencing behavior without removing options."
"    *   *Impact:* Inspired the creation of """"nudge units"""" (e.g., in the UK); paved the way for behavioral economics."
    *   *Other details:* He's 72; won 9 million Swedish krona; appeared in *The Big Short*.

"    *   *Central Message:* _______ _____ (Richard Thaler) '_____ _____' (Nudge theory) ______ _________ ______________ (Behavioral Economics) ______ ___________ ________ _________________ ______ ________ ____________. (Richard Thaler won the Nobel Prize for bringing revolutionary changes to behavioral economics through """"Nudge theory"""".)"
"    *   *Supporting Info 1 (The Concept):* _______ _______ ___________ (rational) _________ ___________, ____ _______ ____ ________ ____ ____ ____ ______ _________ ___ ___________. (He proved that humans don't always make rational decisions and tend to lean towards easy or habitual actions.)"
"    *   *Supporting Info 2 (Nudging):* """"________"""" ___ ______ ______ _______ _______ _________ (________: _______ ____ _____ ___ _____ ____ ___________ _____ _________) __________ __________ _________ _________ ___ __________. (He explained that through """"nudging,"""" people can be subtly influenced to make better decisions, like saving for pensions or eating healthy.)"
    *   *Supporting Info 3 (Impact):* ___ ________ ____ ___________ _____ __________ ___________ '_____ _______'__ _______ ______. (His research led governments to set up 'nudge units' to change public behavior.)

"    *   *Draft:* _______ _____ '_____ _____' (Nudge Theory) ______ _________ ______________ (Behavioral Economics) ___ _____ ________ ______ __________ ______ ________ ____________. _______ _______ ___________ _________ ___________, ______ _______ ____ ________ ____ ____ ____ ______ _________ ___ ___________. ______ _______ _________ (________: _______ ____ ______ _____) __________ """"________"""" ___ ______ ______ __________ _________ _________ ___ __________. ___ ________ _________ ____ ____ ______ _____ __________ ___________ ________ '_____ _________' _______ ______."

