    *   *Subject:* A rare inflammatory syndrome in children (PIMS-TS) that mimics Kawasaki disease.
"    *   *Symptoms:* High fever, rash, red eyes, swelling, general pain, heart/circulation issues, swollen glands, dry lips."
    *   *Age group:* Affects children up to age 16 (unlike Kawasaki which is mostly under 5).
    *   *Link to COVID-19:* Likely a delayed immune response/antibody response to the virus (post-infectious). Occurs 3-6 weeks after infection. Many children test negative for the virus itself but positive for antibodies.
