"    *   *Introduction:* A 2014 survey shows many people can't name a famous female scientist. On the 150th anniversary of Marie Curie's birth, the text highlights other trailblazing women in science."
    *   *Marie Curie:* First double Nobel laureate (Physics and Chemistry). Discovered polonium and radium. First female professor at Sorbonne. Died of radiation exposure.
"    *   *Peggy Whitson:* First science officer on the ISS. PhD in biology/chemistry. Conducts experiments in space (crops, cancer, fluids)."
    *   *Marie Tharp:* First to map the Atlantic Ocean floor. Proved plate tectonics through mapping (despite being dismissed/not being allowed on ships).
"    *   *Wanda Diaz-Merced:* Astrophysicist with vision loss. Developed """"data sonification"""" (converting star data to sound) to make astronomy accessible to visually impaired researchers."
"    *   *Quarraisha Abdool Karim:* Epidemiologist. Researched HIV/AIDS spread in South Africa, specifically its impact on women. Awarded Order of Mapungubwe."
    *   *Soyeon Yi:* First South Korean astronaut. Aimed to inspire more women in science.
    *   *Rajaa Cherkaoui El Moursli:* Nuclear physicist. Played a key role in proving the existence of the Higgs boson. Established the first medical physics master's in Morocco.

    *   *Central Message:* Highlighting the significant contributions of various trailblazing women in science across different fields.
    *   *Supporting Info (Key Figures):*
"        *   Marie Curie (Nobel prizes, radioactivity)."
        *   Peggy Whitson (ISS science officer).
        *   Marie Tharp (Ocean floor mapping).
