    *   *Polishing for natural English:*
"        """"When asked to respond, Miller said, 'There are people listening, Mike talks a lot... I was getting ready, so I didn't really listen to what they were saying.'"""""

"    *   *Contextual check:* In Kannada, """"______________ ____ _____ _____________"""" is a bit ambiguous without context, but it literally means """"There are listeners, Mike talks a lot..."""" or """"There are people listening, and Mike talks a lot..."""". Looking at the sentence structure, it seems to be a quote."

    *   Let's look at the structure again:
"        """"_______ _______ ___________ ________ _______, [Quote] ____ _______."""""
"        """"When asked to respond, Miller said, '[Quote].'"""""

