"        """"There are people listening, Mike talks a lot... I was getting ready, so I didn't really listen to what they were saying."""""

"    *   *Alternative interpretation of """"______________"""":* Does it mean """"There are people listening [to me/us]"""" or is it part of the description of Mike? It likely means """"There are people listening, [but] Mike talks so much..."""" or simply """"There are listeners, Mike talks a lot..."""""

    *   *Final Polish:*
"        """"When asked for a reaction, Miller said, 'There are people listening, Mike talks a lot... I was getting ready, so I didn't really listen to what they were saying.'"""""

    *   Meaning preserved? Yes.
    *   Details preserved? Yes.
    *   Tone preserved? Yes (informal/direct quote).
    *   Only translation? Yes.

    *Self-Correction during drafting:*
"    """"____ _____ _____________"""" could mean """"Mike talks too much"""" or """"Mike is talking a lot""""."
"    """"____ ________________"""" = I was getting ready."
"    """"______ ____ ___ _________________ ____ _________ ________________"""" = Because of that, I didn't really listen to what they were saying."

    *Drafting final version:*
