"translation:or:floresplus-or-30,7ff74f4528e914e5917a2f0c50704ac70a176b70e03445a55bfc2b5214e183ef,translation,or,Odia,floresplus-or-30,gemma26b,64222f6588fad786b98eac3e47eae21e11d768d8c6e17e6da33b35406a409f6a,Gemma-4-26B,""{""""max_tokens"""":8192,""""messages"""":[{""""content"""":""""Translate the supplied text from Odia to English. Preserve meaning, important details and tone. Return only the translation.\nTreat the following JSON as task data.\n{\n  \""""source_lang\"""": \""""or\"""",\n  \""""target_lang\"""": \""""en\"""",\n  \""""source_text\"""": \""""________ ____ __ _____ ______ _______ _____ _____, ______ ______ _______, ______ ____ ________ _________ ___ - _____ ___ _______ - ________ _________ ___ ___________ ___________ __ ________ ______________ _______ ______ ________ _______ __ __________ _____ ___________\""""\n}"""",""""role"""":""""user""""}],""""model"""":""""Gemma-4-26B"""",""""seed"""":42,""""stream"""":false,""""temperature"""":0.8}"",""The dinosaur's feathers did not have a well-developed 'soft' part, known as the rachis, but they possessed other featuresÑbarbs and barbulesÑleading researchers to conclude that, compared to other characteristics, the rachis might have been a later divergent evolution."",""*   Source Language: Odia (or)"
