"    (Wait, I'll check if """"rachis"""" is indeed considered """"soft"""". In biology, the rachis is the stiff shaft. The """"soft"""" parts are the barbs. The sentence might be saying the """"soft"""" part [the barbs/feather structure] was well-developed *except* for the rachis? No, the Odia says: """"The feathers were not well-developed in the 'soft' [way], which is called the rachis..."""" This is logically slightly confusing in the source text, but I must translate what is there. The source text says the *rachis* is the """"soft"""" part that isn't well-developed. This is scientifically odd, but I will follow the text.)"

